"""Abigail Marston, part B: Personality, Skills/weapons/horses, Relationships (19 Oct 2026).

Sources (register): Rockstar character description of 6 Sep 2018 (English text as reprinted by The
Hollywood Reporter / Heat Vision, Sep 2018; French text from rockstargames.com/reddeadredemption2/fr/
features/vanderlindegang, as quoted by the French Red Dead Wiki); Red Dead Redemption 2: The Complete
Official Guide, as quoted by the Red Dead Wiki; a character biography page from an official guide
(scan of the wiki file AbigailRobertsBio.jpg, captioned "Biography in RDR 2" on the wiki, read and
quoted verbatim; the edition is not identified, so it is not called the Collector's Edition); Red
Dead Wiki EN "Abigail Marston" (infobox, Personality, Appearance, Quotes, Trivia) and FR "Abigail
Marston" (trivia: dominoes at eight); wiki pages "Camp Events" (chapters 1 to 4), "Dominoes",
"Uncle" (footnote quoting John in "A Continual Feast"), "Susan Grimshaw", "Molly O'Shea", "Kieran
Duffy", "Orville Swanson", "Simon Pearson", "A New Future Imagined", "Letter from Abigail" (full
text). Transcripts: Outlaws from the West; Enter, Pursued by a Memory; Who the Hell is Leviticus
Cornwall?; Eastward Bound; A Fisher of Men; Red Dead Redemption (mission); American Venom; The
Outlaw's Return; Pestilence; Old Friends, New Problems; The Last Enemy That Shall Be Destroyed; Bear
One Another's Burdens; The Gates of El Presidio; And The Truth Will Set You Free; Great Men Are Not
Always Wise; An Appointed Time. Palmer interviews as established in bill_D (The Nerd Soapbox, 22 May
2019; Retroplayer for The Gaming Liberty, 30 Sep 2010). Fact-checked fiches reused as is: john_A..E,
arthur_A..F, dutch_A..D, sadie_A..D, micah_A..D, hosea_A..D, charles_A..D, bill_A..D, javier_A..D;
live Tilly fiche (letter signed "Tilly Pierre").

Ownership (FIX_RULES): official descriptions (Rockstar 2018, Complete Official Guide, guide
biography page), names (Abigail Roberts, Mrs. Marston, Abby, Agatha Milton, "darling", "my angel"),
appearance (incl. the height difference between games), literacy, dominoes, ranch chores after the
credits, and all camp scenes live HERE. Each camp scene sits in ONE relationship entry only.
Narrative events (Colter, Jack's kidnapping, bank job, Sisika, Van Horn, Pronghorn, Beecher's Hope,
1911 detention, Ross's and Dutch's 1911 lines, the final attack, 1914) live in part A; relationship
entries refer to them in a short clause. Lines quoted under "In her own words" (part C Quotes and
part A must NOT repeat them): "This is a new low, even by your standards."; "Guess I was hoping to
see a corpse."; "I always was a good thief."; "No, John, I don't like it... I love it. It's
home."; "I can take care of myself, John. One guard got funny on me one time..."; "I never was much
of a cook, but I did try to be a good wife."; "Oh, people can change, Miss MacFarlane..."; "The
life we led, that doesn't go away. It's never over." Other lines quoted only here: "loving you means
I can't watch you do this" (letter, Personality), "especially his mother, Abigail" (Rockstar's Jack
description), "and for teachin' the miserable old goat some manners" / "I'm only teasin'. I like
her, and I'm glad she saved your life." (Bonnie), "Bill never did like surprises" (Bill), Micah's
"Without John, she's just bait.", John's "creep" retort (Javier), Swanson's opening line (Davey entry).
Lines kept in part C Quotes and only paraphrased here: "father's useless", "silly bastard ...
sheep", "parasite... you cook", "dumb fools", "An outlaw and a workin' girl", "orphaned working
girl", "You're a rotten man".

WIKI-ONLY (kept, attributed): Agatha Milton alias and Abby nickname (infobox); red roan Tennessee
Walker (infobox); Cattleman Revolver in both games (infobox); dominoes learned in a saloon at eight
(FR wiki); height difference between games (EN wiki trivia); camp-event scenes (paraphrased in our
own wording, no quotation marks except where a transcript exists); Susan "hag" insult (Susan page,
paraphrased); Molly advice (Molly page and Camp Events, paraphrased); Javier's chapter 6 doubts
about her loyalty (per javier_B); Uncle telling her that Arthur thought John lucky to have her, and
her tears (EN wiki trivia; the FR wiki says Uncle tells John, so it is attributed to the EN wiki).

Excluded: Arthur's journal entry saying he should have married her (wiki trivia, no transcript, reads
as interpretation); "Bill and Javier wanted to be with Abigail" (wiki "implied"); Abigail's
"several relationships with gang members" (FR wiki "il est dit", rumour); Uncle's absent-grave theory;
Etta Place / Crucible / Adams comparisons (part C trivia); RDR1 multiplayer model and outfits (part
C); Cali Elizabeth Moore and Sophia Marzocchi (part D); Abigail "jealous" (wiki reading; her own
"I ain't jealous so much as curious" stands as the fact, paraphrased); "Abigail shoots in 1911" (no
source: in "The Last Enemy" only John, Uncle and Jack fire); laundry and camp cooking in 1899 (no
source); the "Abby darlin'" form (no transcript found); the claim that the game's mission credits
call her Abigail Roberts (no source found, cut after fact-check); Bill insulting Abigail and Jack
at Fort Mercer (not in the "Exodus in America" transcript, cut); Hosea's "down south" and "make
plans" wording (Camp Events summary, not a transcript: paraphrased without quotation marks).
Hosea's "best actress" is kept in the Hosea entry only, paraphrased. Live-site errors spotted (not
fixed here): the Bonnie fiche says she meets Abigail while herding cattle (it is in "Old Friends, New
Problems"), the Andrew Milton fiche says Abigail kills him at Beaver Hollow (it is at Van Horn).
Consistency flag: micah_B places Micah's "father to Jack" advance at Clemens Point (FR wiki); the EN
Camp Events page puts it at Horseshoe Overlook, which this fiche follows.
"""

